      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> There is a forwarding rule in the mail server config pointing at a BridgeWorks address, and I would rather understand that service than point a scanner at it. A mail server tends to volunteer more than it means to during the opening exchange, before anyone has authenticated to anything. I want to see for myself what this one admits to supporting.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>nc mail.hallowayprecision.com 25</b>, then greet the service with <b>EHLO cordatasecurity.com</b>.",
      "taskQuestion": "Which command in the server's capability list can be used to check whether a user exists?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> VRFY is advertised in the EHLO response. Its reply still has to be interpreted; availability does not guarantee a definitive answer."
    },
    {
      "answers": [
        "EHLO",
        "VRFY",
