        "DSN"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> A mail server that answers questions about who exists will build a target list for you at no charge. The trick is knowing which verb to trust, and that starts with what the service says about itself before anybody logs in. Do this one by hand: a scanner hands you a summary and swallows the part that matters.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>nc mail.hallowayprecision.com 25</b>, then greet the service with <b>EHLO cordatasecurity.com</b>.",
      "taskQuestion": "Which command in the server's capability list can be used to check whether a user exists?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> VRFY is available, but the numeric reply determines whether it reveals anything useful."
    },
